So for this, we have a
diamond drill, a drill, some water,

00:27:25.958 --> 00:27:28.375
and a leftover piece
that apparently needs to go

00:27:28.458 --> 00:27:29.916
underneath the granite to make sure

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.583
it doesn't crack when you go through.

00:28:10.333 --> 00:28:11.541
So if you put in a screw now,

00:28:12.041 --> 00:28:13.708
it still sticks out a little bit here.

00:28:14.791 --> 00:28:17.291
So we're gonna give it a
little chamfer with a bigger drill.

00:28:28.166 --> 00:28:29.958
But actually one
much smoother than expected.

00:28:30.500 --> 00:28:33.416
So I guess we're just
gonna continue drilling all of them.

00:29:02.833 --> 00:29:04.000
So we're currently in the house,

00:29:04.166 --> 00:29:05.375
brought the granite here,

00:29:05.458 --> 00:29:07.416
and we need to install all of this.

00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:09.291
So it's gonna be a bit of puzzling,

00:29:09.375 --> 00:29:10.583
especially around the chimney.

00:29:10.666 --> 00:29:12.125
It's gonna be harder
because it would still need

00:29:12.208 --> 00:29:14.083
to cut the granite to work around it.

00:29:15.041 --> 00:29:17.541
And so it's just gonna
be a bit of a freestyle puzzle

00:29:17.833 --> 00:29:19.083
to cover off the wall.

00:29:19.500 --> 00:29:21.541
So we're gonna take a piece of granite.

00:29:22.375 --> 00:29:24.208
They're all in very different sizes.

00:29:24.791 --> 00:29:28.583
So we're roughly gonna
hammer it here in the right size.

00:29:33.458 --> 00:29:36.708
Once the size is
good, we're gonna put them here.

00:29:38.666 --> 00:29:40.833
The first piece is a bit of a rough one,

00:29:41.083 --> 00:29:42.166
just because it's cool.

00:29:49.666 --> 00:29:51.416
And on the bottom, we don't have a hole

00:29:51.500 --> 00:29:53.416
because it was a
bit too much work to drill.

00:29:54.041 --> 00:29:56.791
So we're gonna use some leftover wood

00:29:57.416 --> 00:29:58.333
to chop a little block.

00:29:58.583 --> 00:30:00.333
It's really just a simple little block.

00:30:00.625 --> 00:30:01.791
And this is gonna go on the bottom

00:30:01.875 --> 00:30:04.416
to secure the granite
and make sure it stays in place.

00:30:05.375 --> 00:30:08.250
And later, once all the granite is in,

00:30:08.333 --> 00:30:10.291
we're gonna build a
little bit of a platform

00:30:10.375 --> 00:30:11.583
where the stove will be on.

00:30:12.083 --> 00:30:13.708
So the blocks will be covered.

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:40.916
So now comes the most challenging part,

00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:42.541
going around the chimney pipe

00:30:43.458 --> 00:30:44.750
because it means cutting the granite

00:30:44.833 --> 00:30:46.208
and drilling a few extra holes.

00:30:47.250 --> 00:30:49.166
But luckily, I already did that.

00:30:49.583 --> 00:30:51.500
So now we can just assemble everything

00:30:51.625 --> 00:30:52.958
and hopefully it fits.

00:31:03.250 --> 00:31:04.166
So far so good.

00:31:04.250 --> 00:31:06.125
I think we're going a little bit angled

00:31:06.333 --> 00:31:08.416
because this one is not super straight.

00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:09.708
But I think it should be okay.

00:31:25.666 --> 00:31:26.416
Cool, all fits.

00:31:26.750 --> 00:31:29.458
Next, you need to put
these little blocks on the bottom

00:31:29.541 --> 00:31:31.041
to make sure they're secure.

00:31:37.375 --> 00:31:38.333
So here's the chimney hole.

00:31:38.750 --> 00:31:41.375
As you can see, it's cutted around it,

00:31:41.458 --> 00:31:42.541
but not super accurate.

00:31:42.875 --> 00:31:44.375
Not a pro granite cutter yet.

00:31:45.333 --> 00:31:46.791
But luckily it's very common thing

00:31:46.875 --> 00:31:48.583
that is hard to go
around the chimney pipe.

00:31:48.666 --> 00:31:51.291
So you have these things to cover it up.

00:31:56.541 --> 00:31:57.875
Not sure if I like that thing,

00:31:57.958 --> 00:31:59.291
but it should be functional now.

00:31:59.500 --> 00:32:00.958
So the wall is in place.

00:32:01.625 --> 00:32:03.000
Next, we're gonna make the bottom part.

00:32:03.500 --> 00:32:04.833
This is gonna be a little bit challenging

00:32:05.000 --> 00:32:07.375
because I didn't wanna
drill too many holes in the granite.

00:32:09.083 --> 00:32:12.375
So the floor is
gonna be against the granite.

00:32:13.166 --> 00:32:14.000
But as you can see,

00:32:14.083 --> 00:32:16.041
the granite all
has different thicknesses.

00:32:16.458 --> 00:32:18.375
So we need to make the bottom plate

00:32:18.458 --> 00:32:20.541
and cut out all the edges

00:32:20.750 --> 00:32:22.833
of the different granite thicknesses,

00:32:23.375 --> 00:32:27.666
which I think still is
easier than cutting all the granite,

00:32:27.958 --> 00:32:29.958
but I'm not sure how
this next step is gonna be.

00:32:30.791 --> 00:32:31.958
So for the floor,

00:32:32.083 --> 00:32:34.250
we're gonna use some leftover metal

00:32:34.333 --> 00:32:36.000
that was originally in the trailer.

00:32:36.916 --> 00:32:38.541
Right there is the pile I had in mind.

00:32:41.916 --> 00:32:43.375
And there's this big aluminum sheet.

00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:47.083
So it is the front
side with the relive up,

00:32:47.333 --> 00:32:48.375
Hard to clean.

00:32:48.791 --> 00:32:49.375
This is the back.

00:32:49.708 --> 00:32:51.750
You still see the
pattern, but it's smooth.

00:32:52.541 --> 00:32:53.958
So it should be a bit more convenient.

00:33:34.708 --> 00:33:36.416
So now I'm gonna
measure all the granite pieces

00:33:36.833 --> 00:33:40.208
and draw them all
in so we can cut it out.

00:33:44.000 --> 00:33:45.125
After taking the measures,

00:33:45.458 --> 00:33:47.833
I started cutting
and fitting the metal sheet.

00:33:51.208 --> 00:33:51.916
Then some polishing.

00:33:54.500 --> 00:33:56.541
And I built a base
with some wooden leftovers.

00:34:01.166 --> 00:34:02.583
Still had to drill some more holes

00:34:02.666 --> 00:34:04.250
to attach the metal sheet to the base.

00:34:13.708 --> 00:34:16.125
And last, some wood
finishing for the edges.

00:34:23.291 --> 00:34:24.875
So the area for the stove is now ready.

00:34:25.416 --> 00:34:28.916
Aluminum sheet here,
wooden finishing around it.

00:34:29.625 --> 00:34:31.666
So next step is to install the stove,

00:34:31.750 --> 00:34:32.916
but first we need to clean it up

00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:34.333
and I'm gonna get some help for that.

00:34:35.208 --> 00:34:35.708
Yeah.

00:34:36.666 --> 00:34:38.916
I got this stove from someone last year.

00:34:39.125 --> 00:34:41.708
Has been outside for the whole year,

00:34:41.791 --> 00:34:45.708
so we need to do
something with it, try to repair it.

00:34:46.083 --> 00:34:47.541
Legs are very rusty.

00:34:48.125 --> 00:34:49.166
We need to clean the glass.

00:34:51.333 --> 00:34:52.875
Some screws missing.

00:34:54.875 --> 00:34:55.625
And clean the inside.

00:35:52.041 --> 00:35:53.916
Okay, now we have heat in the house.

00:35:54.208 --> 00:35:56.291
Quite essential for
the dark and cold winter nights

00:35:56.375 --> 00:35:56.958
that are coming.

00:35:57.791 --> 00:35:59.208
Also quite essential is light.

00:35:59.541 --> 00:36:01.166
And for that, we need light switches.

00:36:03.291 --> 00:36:05.041
They're actually
pretty hard to find secondhand.

00:36:05.500 --> 00:36:06.500
It always feels a bit painful

00:36:06.583 --> 00:36:08.083
having to buy this from new plastic,

00:36:08.750 --> 00:36:09.958
especially knowing that we're gonna need

00:36:10.125 --> 00:36:11.458
many more of those in the future.

00:36:12.458 --> 00:36:14.416
So a few months ago, we put out a call

00:36:14.500 --> 00:36:16.791
to Precious Plastic
Community to try and develop one

00:36:16.875 --> 00:36:17.750
in a little contest.

00:36:18.458 --> 00:36:20.291
For anyone that is able to make a mold,

00:36:20.791 --> 00:36:22.708
to inject with a Precious Plastic machine,

00:36:23.208 --> 00:36:24.333
you can get a thousand euros

00:36:24.416 --> 00:36:27.750
for the first one that
shows us a working light switch.

00:36:28.083 --> 00:36:28.833
And we had a winner.

00:36:29.625 --> 00:36:31.916
So we just received
the package from Johannplasto

00:36:32.208 --> 00:36:33.750
from Germany and he made

00:36:34.166 --> 00:36:37.166
some cool light switches.

00:36:39.041 --> 00:36:42.375
Nice, he says like
how much plastic we recycled.

00:36:42.916 --> 00:36:44.458
342 grams.

00:36:45.125 --> 00:36:47.333
He also has a
website, make sure to check it out.

00:36:47.416 --> 00:36:48.458
Look nicely packed.

00:36:49.791 --> 00:36:51.125
Here's the first type of switch.

00:36:51.666 --> 00:36:52.541
Looks really nice.

00:36:55.083 --> 00:36:56.000
And here's another type.

00:36:56.291 --> 00:36:57.041
It's a bit bigger.

00:36:58.416 --> 00:36:59.875
All are made from polypropylene.

00:37:01.125 --> 00:37:02.541
And the difference is that one--

00:37:02.625 --> 00:37:04.500
gets in the wall, so it's covered.

00:37:05.250 --> 00:37:07.875
And one with an
enclosure, so it's an outside switch.

00:37:08.333 --> 00:37:10.500
So you can mount it when
you don't have a double wall.

00:37:12.958 --> 00:37:14.833
Let's see what they
look like when we open them up.

00:37:15.583 --> 00:37:18.000
Three injected
parts made with precious plastic

00:37:18.291 --> 00:37:19.583
and one off-the-shelf piece

00:37:19.875 --> 00:37:21.458
to make sure it all functions well.

00:37:29.375 --> 00:37:30.375
Here you can see how they're made.

00:37:31.166 --> 00:37:33.375
First making a 3D
model with the exact sizes.

00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:35.791
Then a 3D printer mold is used

00:37:35.875 --> 00:37:37.250
so you can make a quick injection

00:37:37.875 --> 00:37:39.458
to see if all the
measurements are correct.

00:37:44.083 --> 00:37:45.833
And overall, this
is still a first prototype

00:37:45.916 --> 00:37:47.333
to see if everything works properly.

00:37:48.083 --> 00:37:50.250
And you can download all
the drawings open source online

00:37:50.333 --> 00:37:52.541
in the precious plastic
community if you want to replicate it.

00:37:53.291 --> 00:37:55.875
For now, we're going to
install them and see how they work.

00:37:56.625 --> 00:37:58.958
Hopefully all good and
we can make a final proper mold

00:37:59.041 --> 00:38:01.000
so we can use it in
Project Kamp for the long term.

00:38:01.708 --> 00:38:04.166
Injecting our own
plastic waste into useful items.

00:38:05.958 --> 00:38:07.541
Now, Adrián will install them.

00:38:45.500 --> 00:38:47.291
So, let's see if it works.

00:38:52.333 --> 00:38:53.875
It works, looks nice.

00:38:54.583 --> 00:38:56.208
But we noticed some little details

00:38:56.291 --> 00:38:57.833
that maybe doesn't work that good.

00:38:57.916 --> 00:38:58.833
It's still a prototype.

00:38:59.416 --> 00:39:00.916
You've seen how the mold is done.

00:39:01.125 --> 00:39:02.666
So it's the version one of this.

00:39:03.666 --> 00:39:05.083
It wiggles a bit here.

00:39:05.166 --> 00:39:09.083
And we noticed that
probably the fitting of these pieces

00:39:09.166 --> 00:39:11.000
is not perfect in these holes.

00:39:12.583 --> 00:39:14.291
Normal when you
work with these materials.

00:39:15.708 --> 00:39:17.291
But we will keep on using it.

00:39:17.500 --> 00:39:19.166
Try it out because
that's what we do here.

00:39:19.375 --> 00:39:20.041
Try out things.

00:39:20.833 --> 00:39:22.791
And try to improve it in the future

00:39:22.958 --> 00:39:27.500
to see if we can
make something very satisfying

00:39:27.750 --> 00:39:30.208
to press.

00:39:34.166 --> 00:39:36.666
Happy to see Precious
Plastic being useful in Project kamp.

00:39:37.208 --> 00:39:39.041
And also happy we're
getting closer to the end.

00:39:39.375 --> 00:39:41.791
We just need to take
care of a few more final details.

00:39:42.250 --> 00:39:44.291
And we still have
two problems with the door.

00:39:44.625 --> 00:39:47.416
One is that we don't
have anything to open it up.

00:39:48.916 --> 00:39:50.416
So at the moment we use a screwdriver.

00:39:52.000 --> 00:39:53.916
And second, this doesn't lock properly

00:39:54.291 --> 00:39:56.000
because it's just this piece of wood

00:39:56.291 --> 00:39:58.041
which probably is
gonna wear out over time.

00:39:58.291 --> 00:39:59.625
So it's better if there's some metal

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:01.541
on there to lock the door properly.

00:40:02.541 --> 00:40:04.458
So I found this
nice piece of stainless steel

00:40:04.541 --> 00:40:05.708
from a broken spatula.

00:40:06.041 --> 00:40:07.958
Used to be one of
these things in the kitchen

00:40:08.208 --> 00:40:10.333
to flip the food like
SpongeBob on his burgers

00:40:10.833 --> 00:40:13.541
But it broke over here on the edge.

00:40:13.958 --> 00:40:15.250
No problem, we got a new one.

00:40:15.333 --> 00:40:17.416
But now I can use this piece of metal

00:40:17.583 --> 00:40:19.166
to make the holder for the door.

00:40:20.000 --> 00:40:21.958
So it's gonna be something like this

00:40:23.083 --> 00:40:25.666
with a hole inside
for the door to lock in.

00:40:26.208 --> 00:40:29.416
And two screws so we can attach it.

00:40:53.000 --> 00:40:54.958
Next, we're gonna
use this leftover material

00:40:55.250 --> 00:40:57.875
from the pig trailer
to make a little door handle.

00:41:55.416 --> 00:41:56.750
Okay, door handle done.

00:41:57.708 --> 00:41:59.083
We just need some finished touches

00:41:59.333 --> 00:42:01.666
and Julien seems the right guy to do it.

00:42:02.333 --> 00:42:05.125
Here we have a little space, little gap.

00:42:06.125 --> 00:42:06.708
Just like here.

00:42:07.625 --> 00:42:11.583
I have already cut this piece

00:42:11.708 --> 00:42:16.875
because it comes from a bigger leftover.

00:42:17.708 --> 00:42:18.500
Just this part.

00:42:19.375 --> 00:42:22.083
Cut, screw, and it's done.

00:42:30.958 --> 00:42:31.833
That was easy.

00:42:32.458 --> 00:42:33.500
Next room now.

00:42:38.833 --> 00:42:39.625
It's done.

00:42:40.708 --> 00:42:44.083
So here, you can see we have a gap

00:42:44.291 --> 00:42:46.541
between the paneling and the window.

00:42:47.541 --> 00:42:52.375
So now we need to put some little pieces

00:42:52.583 --> 00:42:53.458
of wood.

00:43:17.333 --> 00:43:18.916
The pieces of wood are cut.

00:43:19.708 --> 00:43:25.291
Now I need to cut the side of the window.

00:44:13.625 --> 00:44:14.458
It's cold.

00:44:20.916 --> 00:44:23.791
I'm gonna sand all of this piece of wood

00:44:24.333 --> 00:44:26.625
inside the room so it's not really good.

00:44:27.958 --> 00:44:31.041
That's why ear protection, mask,

00:44:32.500 --> 00:44:34.125
it's never too much against the dust.

00:45:48.416 --> 00:45:48.916
Okay.

00:45:51.208 --> 00:45:57.583
So the edge of the door is finished.

00:46:00.416 --> 00:46:01.250
Everything is finished.

00:46:02.000 --> 00:46:04.000
All the finishing are finished.

00:46:06.083 --> 00:46:06.583
So,

00:46:10.083 --> 00:46:10.625
see you.

00:46:21.916 --> 00:46:23.833
Okay, we just finished the building,

00:46:23.916 --> 00:46:25.750
but we still need to clean a bit.

00:47:07.125 --> 00:47:08.791
And now the pig trailer is finished,

00:47:09.291 --> 00:47:11.125
ready to be used
by the team in the winter.

00:47:11.666 --> 00:47:13.791
It has been an
adventure and we learned a lot

00:47:13.875 --> 00:47:15.666
on how to renovate and build with reuse

00:47:15.750 --> 00:47:16.791
and recycled materials.

00:47:17.791 --> 00:47:20.000
It certainly brings
limitations and challenges

00:47:20.750 --> 00:47:23.208
and sometimes you have
to go through the usual way,

00:47:23.958 --> 00:47:26.208
but we will keep
improving in the projects to come.

00:47:59.875 --> 00:48:01.458
And that was it for this update.

00:48:01.708 --> 00:48:03.625
The next one will
be the last of this season,

00:48:03.875 --> 00:48:05.958
where we are going
to do some big land works

00:48:06.083 --> 00:48:07.958
before the winter comes, everybody leaves

00:48:08.166 --> 00:48:09.083
and the rain takes over.

00:48:09.708 --> 00:48:11.333
If you want to see it right now,

00:48:11.416 --> 00:48:13.750
you can support us in
Patreon and in the future,

00:48:13.875 --> 00:48:15.833
probably be part of the decision making,

00:48:15.916 --> 00:48:18.458
like the choosing of
the colors of this pig trailer.

00:48:18.791 --> 00:48:20.875
If not, you can
subscribe to the YouTube channel.

00:48:21.375 --> 00:48:23.333
Thanks for watching
and see you in the next update.

